 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+### Browser agent tools
+
+WebMCP-capable browsers can discover these client-side tools on every page:
+
+- `list_articles`: return article slugs, titles, and summaries.
+- `get_article`: return metadata and full article text for a known slug.
+- `get_reading_list`: return saved articles for the current browser session.
+- `open_search`: open the search flyout and expose its `search_articles` form tool.
+- `open_reading_list`: open the reading-list flyout and expose its
+  `toggle_reading_list` form tool. Selecting a saved article removes it; selecting
+  an unsaved article saves it.
+
+Form tools return JSON results through the native submission event's
+`respondWith` method. They are available while their flyouts are open. Imperative
+registration uses `use-webmcp-tool` for feature detection and automatic
+AbortSignal cleanup when Astro navigation unmounts the React islands. Network
+utilities forward execution cancellation signals and use the existing same-origin
+article and session endpoints. Browsers without WebMCP retain the standard forms
+and buttons. WebMCP availability depends on browser support and a secure context.
